+# Device-only receipt queue store (#699, partial infrastructure)
+
+Refs #699, dependent on upload-intent API #698. Parent #559 owner decision:
+“Ja: Offline-Belegdateien mit separatem Retry ergänzen”. These three new files
+supply a separate IndexedDB Blob store and eight positive native storage cases and an explicit ephemeral-capability case.
+No receipt UI, multipart transport, auth or logout integration is wired yet;
+#699, #700 and parent #559 remain incomplete.
+
+An explicit selection commits a fresh key, immutable original Blob, filename,
+possibly empty camera MIME and optional already-saved booking target before
+transport may use it. Status functions require request-start epoch/generation
+provenance and cannot replace the payload/key. Uncertainty remains set until a
+validated acknowledgment deletes the intent. Cleanup failure retains it. A
+separate file-delivery Web Lock leaves the text-booking queue/lock untouched;
+its page-local fallback relies on server #698 idempotency across tabs. Existing
+nonempty/15 MiB bounds apply; server signature/type/metadata stripping remains
+authoritative. No cookie, token, raw file, filename or booking target enters
+localStorage or Cache Storage. This is plaintext same-origin device storage,
+not encryption or a cached authentication claim.
+
+## Explicit privacy intents and storage failures
+
+Every public raw-access guard verifies localStorage write/read/remove capability,
+not merely a readable matching epoch. Only random nonfinancial probe/epoch/hold
+markers use that storage. A late notification for an epoch already observed by
+a fresh token is harmless; new epochs/holds still fence old callbacks.
+
+`holdReceiptQueueForSignOut()` invalidates the current context synchronously,
+broadcasts an intent and immediately starts a uniquely owned native hold in the
+existing `meta` store. Its awaitable `ready` reports native persistence and
+whether the independent localStorage fence succeeded. Every initialization and
+raw-read/write transaction checks native pending holds, so a cold sibling that
+missed the broadcast cannot access old files after localStorage becomes writable
+again. A failed LS marker never claims a durable LS fence. Native metadata is the
+fallback, with no extra database or auth protocol.
+
+The #700 caller must start `clear()` immediately on explicit logout intent,
+independently of HTTP. Clear erases raw intents and advances the native epoch in
+one transaction while preserving **all** privacy holds. It reports actual native
+commit and whether the LS epoch updated. After clear and HTTP completion, await
+`release()` to complete only this handle's hold. Failed/crashed native fences or
+clears remain failed/held; no TTL releases them. If both durable writes are denied,
+no physical erasure or persistent fence is promised and no successful cleanup or
+recovery may be reported. Existing text capture, preferences and other databases
+are outside this wipe.
+
+#700 must call `prepareReceiptQueueRecovery()` **before starting** login, recovery
+or logout HTTP. Its completed native snapshot defines captured old IDs. The
